    "lawCode": "Amd §409-a, Soc Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Social Services Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8421A\n\nSPONSOR: PERSAUD\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the social services law, in relation to reporting data\non child welfare preventive services\n\n \nPURPOSE OF THE BILL:\n\nThis bill would establish reporting requirements for the Office of Chil-\ndren and Family Services to collect data on the utilization and effec-\ntiveness of preventive services throughout the state.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of the bill would amend section 409-a of the Social Services\nLaw by adding a new subdivision that creates annual reporting require-\nments for the Office of Children and Family Services (OCFS) on child\nwelfare preventive services. Reporting requirements would include:\n\n-the total number of children and families receiving preventive services\nat the end of each month;\n\n-the total annual number of unduplicated children and families receiving\npreventive services along with the number of new preventive cases that\nwere opened during the preceding calendar year with the referral source;\n\n-the average length of time preventative services were provided for each\nchild or family during the preceding calendar year including an indi-\ncation of whether the case was closed during such year;\n\n-a descriptive list of all services and their rates of utilization in\neach local social services district that utilize preventive services\nfunding;\n\n-a descriptive list of all other services including primary preventive\nservices funded through the community optional preventive services\nfund,home visiting funds or any other state or local funds, and their\nrates of utilization in each local social services district that does\nnot utilize preventive services funding;\n\n-the number of children who entered the foster care system that received\npreventive services in the year prior to entry;\n\n-any other information deemed necessary by the OCFS Commissioner to\ninclude in such report. Reports would be required to be submitted to the\nGovernor, Speaker of the Assembly, Temporary President of the Senate,\nchairpersons of the Assembly and Senate committees on Children and Fami-\nlies, chairperson ofthe Assembly Ways and Means committee and the chair-\nperson of the Senate Finance committee beginning no later than September\nfirst, two thousand twenty-one.\n\nSection two of the bill would require the bill to take effect immediate-\nly.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\n\nGiven the current climate, many families are under ever increasing\nstress due to the health, mental health, social, and economic challenges\nthat COVID-19 presents. Gathering data on preventive services for chil-\ndren and their families during this crisis and beyond is of great impor-\ntance.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is new legislation.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS TO STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
